t(29, 1985, """O young men, newly married:

You are not alone in loving your mothers; I too am like you. I have a mother, even though she has gone before me to Allah the Exalted. So I, like you, realize the sanctity of the mother in a man's chest, and I know very well what a mother means. I praise Allah the Exalted that my mother left this world and departed it without, God willing, being involved in what some mothers do today.

O young man:
Beware of letting your mother's standing diminish, waver or fall in your heart; beware!

But also, when you take people's daughter from her family's house, know what your religion tells you:
🔴 It is not your wife's duty to serve your mother, except with her consent and out of love, and that is a kindness from her, not a religious duty.
🔴 Your wife has a right in Sharia to a house of her own.
🔴 Your wife has a right in Sharia that your family treat her kindly, and she owes what she is owed.
🔴 If it is established by the judgment of a sane, wise person that your wife is wronged and your family are unjust to her, or that their living together is impossible,""")

t(30, 60, """then it is your wife's right not to visit them, for they are not her kin (the merit of marrying distant relations), and it is their right not to visit her, and let everyone bear the cost of that; yes, it has a cost, and because it has a cost we always say: we fear Allah and try to live together.

In summary .. look upon your mother with as great a reverence as you wish, and write seas of poetry about her; by Allah, no one will blame you except a fool or an aggressive ignoramus, because your wife too reveres her mother in her own way. So do not insult her mother, do not wrong her and do not belittle her, because your wife never does that to your mother.

At the same time, know your wife's rights specific to her as a wife, rights that in reality do not overlap at all with your mother's rights; there is basically no link between the two kinds of rights. Give them to her; she has rights like those upon her, according to what is fitting. And leave behind customs that have manufactured injustice on earth and entrenched it, until we no longer know whether many people worship Allah the Exalted, who sent down the law, or worship the so-called "elder" of the family, and the tribal chief who perhaps says nothing but falsehood, commands nothing but foolishness, and rules only out of ignorance and misguidance?!

If you worship Allah alone, what is the proof of that in your conduct and in your life?! Know that the matter is not proven by words.""")

h(30, 1000, """O young men: listen to me well!""")

t(30, 1690, """Among bees there is a network of biological and chemical ((instant)) communications. The queen (the ya'sub) is the regulator of the hive's rhythm through her scent and hormones, and the worker bees pass these signals on as if they were living internet lines, which makes thousands of bees move in miraculous coordination, without any error, as if programmed by one mind.

When the scout bee finds a place for a new shelter or a rich food source, she returns to the hive and performs a precise geometric "waggle dance", in which she specifies for the other bees the flight angle relative to the sun and the required distance with extreme precision.

Orders and warnings of a danger inside the hive are transmitted through precise mechanical vibrations at specific frequencies, which the bees sense with their legs and antennae.

When the workers wash and feed the queen, a substance from the queen's body clings to the workers' bodies, then the workers pass it from bee to bee with astonishing speed through touch and taste inside the dark hive.

Its effect: this substance is what "informs" every bee that the queen is present and well. If the queen dies or is lost, the flow of this substance stops suddenly, and within only a few hours (not days) the whole hive is struck by severe agitation and audible crying, and the workers immediately begin building emergency new royal cells.

This is a small part of the outpouring of the miraculousness of our Almighty Lord in His creation of the bees; exalted and high is He, greatly exalted, every name of His is holy, and blessed is He in His mighty dominion. Is the matter only in bees? No

It is also in humans .. I do not know how widespread it is, because this is among what is hidden from our perception, for humans are everywhere and it is impossible to talk to them all to measure the matter. But this is my daily and repeated experience over years,""")

t(31, 60, """and it is a real experience I am sure of; I have no doubt about it.

Follow this same post; I will complete it, God willing

We continue, God willing .. Divine programming .. and human programming .. the great power of God; this is so that you know who Allah is

Humans, 7000 years, 10000 years or a million years after their existence .. it does not matter how many years, that is not our subject .. but after all these thousands of years humans have reached what you see today .. sending text and voice messages .. So will they reach divine programming? They lose if they think they are able.

What is the bee experience I have been living for years? I present it for the shaken, the fearful and the trembling, who, God willing, are not among the people of this channel: those trembling at "tomorrow", fearful of "tomorrow" and terrified of "tomorrow". I thank my Almighty Lord that none of those close to me around me are among them, and, thinking well of my Lord, I hold that the people of this gathering are not among them, God willing. But it is knowledge and understanding that will benefit those coming from outside this gathering.

And how will certainty in Allah the Exalted be known and settle in hearts if we do not speak of it, reveal it and not hide it? So people, while they are being shaped, will grasp what helps them better understand Allah, our Almighty Lord, and His power.

The experience
Ongoing, present, established for some years, not months!
Its parties: among those personally close. Not one, two or three, but more than that.
Nature of the experience with close people: instant communication, and I stress the word instant, around the clock. Those close ones sense, in degrees, my time of joy, my time of sadness, my time of anger, my time of exhaustion, the time of all my emotions, and (((((what I am thinking and what I want))))). And most astonishing, sensing all this in many situations minutes, hours or a day before the state happens! And the accuracy of the sensing is 100%

Nature of the experience with those not close (complete strangers): this is repeated often, not rarely, and it is the effect of the desire for something "righteous" to happen, so that righteous desire is reflected at once onto people far away.
Example: yesterday I slept early after failed attempts for days. Allah the Exalted granted me yesterday the ability to sleep after the Isha prayer, and just as I was about to doze off, the doorbell rang. Great distress struck me, because I knew I would not sleep until after Fajr, and so it was. Since the time between Fajr and the Friday prayer was relatively few hours, I woke in a hard state, for reasons too long to explain that make little sleep not enough to wake the mind. I went to the Friday prayer with extreme difficulty, and when the prayer was called and before entering it, I said in my heart: O Lord, let the imam recite short surahs. In the first rak'ah he recited Surah al-Duha, which is not a long surah, and an imam is not known to recite half of it; imams usually complete it. Yet the shaykh, may Allah preserve him, recited some of its verses very fast and in succession without pausing, and bowed before he had even reached half of it! Then in the second rak'ah he recited Surah al-Ikhlas. And many situations with strangers outside the setting of prayer and worship have recurred in the same direction.

Nature of the experience with destinies and situations: in situations and destinies there occur, to a high degree reaching 90 to 95%, coincidences between the heart's desire and what happens, in divine miracles, many of them contrary to reason and to the logic of how things happen. It is not merely a matter of answered supplication; it is merely the desire for something to happen falling into the heart. Supplication is another matter; I say with all impartiality that by Allah the Exalted's grace I supplicate a great deal, and it is answered, and sometimes it is not. Far be it from Allah that I should claim to be one whose supplication is answered in every case.

This post .. what is the reason for publishing it?
By Allah the Exalted's grace, many elements came together that helped and enabled me to write this post. Coming back from the Friday prayer today, I had thought of putting these meanings within the framework of making Allah the Exalted known, but I said: if Allah the Exalted enables me to write it in the way I feel will achieve its required aim, I will publish it.

With this post I want one thing to reach the reader

Allah the Exalted: His power is greater than the internet, greater than satellites, greater than money and the earthly means, and greater than every human organizational movement that people think extraordinary, mighty, awe-inspiring and without a gap!

All human means are empty talk, merely an illusion in people's minds. Whoever wants to know the truth of how the world really runs should read this post well with his heart and awareness, not with his eyes.

Allah .. or nothing""")

