t(33, 405, """For one man, and not for the sake of those with him!

If only those who insist on loving Allah little would understand this post, so that they come to love Allah the Exalted very much, not little. Do you see the extent and magnitude of love in the following hadith:

From Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "A refugee will seek refuge in the House, and an army will be sent against him; when they are in a desert plain of the earth, they will be swallowed up .. to the end of the noble hadith."

Can we understand the meaning of Allah the Exalted loving the one He loves?

An entire army is swallowed up for his sake?!!
And the swallowing itself is among the major signs?!

What love is this? An entire army swallowed up?! And the protection that befalls this man is placed among the major signs of the Hour, not merely a great event?!

The event itself is great, mighty and earth-shaking even if it were not among the major signs of the Hour, yet it was made one of the major signs of the Hour!!

What love is this .. it is no ordinary rescue

Do you understand, my dear reader brother .. my noble reader sister .. do you now understand what you can obtain if Allah the Exalted loves you? Have you now understood the meaning of Allah loving you? Have you now understood how, if Allah loves you, He gives you what minds cannot imagine, and you are pampered in His dominion?!

Have you ever heard of such pampering?! Destiny could have been the meeting of two armies and the victory of the one Allah the Exalted chose, but the time is a different time.

Our Almighty Lord loved the Prophet ﷺ with a great love, protected him and guarded him from dangers with signs, and out of His love for him, Glorified and Exalted is He, He made him prostrate where no human before him had reached, at that great place on the night of the Ascension.

Let no one say that my words mean I am saying the coming historical figure is more beloved to our Almighty Lord than the Prophet ﷺ; that is a lie and a slander. But I say he is beloved to Allah the Almighty in this time and honored, because he is from the Seal of the Prophets ﷺ.

As for the post, it has one aim with no second: to turn your noble attention to Allah .. the one and only Beloved .. the one true love .. the One who holds sway over spirit, soul and body .. love Him as I claim that man loves Him. I hope I have striven in loving Him and striven in speaking of Him, Majestic and Exalted, Mighty and Holy is He.

That is His love when He loves .. look what happened when He loved?!

Mighty in His dominion, All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit. By His grace we were created, by His grace He made us prostrate to Him, by His grace we knew, by His grace we were guided, by His grace we were protected, by His grace we were saved, by His grace He gave us, healed us and provided for us. None falls short in loving Him except one who is tempted, none is heedless of loving Him except one who is deprived, and none is denied His love except one who is forsaken.""")

