t(34, 1740, """This wording has been graded sound by a number of major hadith scholars, and I believe the wording is sound in its chain to the Prophet ﷺ for these reasons:
🟢 The wording runs clearly and coherently with the event and fits it, for he is the one appointed and installed by Allah the Exalted directly, not by any of the creation. So the meaning clear to everyone of sound thinking and keen mind is that the One who appoints and installs to this position is Allah the Exalted directly, and so he was described with this description, as if you said, and to Allah belongs the highest example, "Ahmad is the one installed and appointed by President so-and-so", combining the name of the appointer who ordered the installation and appointment with the one who was appointed.
🟢 Because he receives guidance directly from Allah the Exalted, and the Guide is Allah. He is certainly enlightened by the Book and the Sunnah, but he is guided to understand what people find difficult in them only because Allah the Exalted guides him directly. In our time people have split into groups and parties; one says the meaning of Allah the Exalted's word on such-and-such is this, and another says no, it is such-and-such. This understanding runs firmly and clearly side by side with his established description as "the Mahdi". So whose Mahdi (guided one) is he? The Mahdi of the political Islam groups? Never, far from it! Or the Mahdi of the Sufis? Never, far from it! Because he is guided by Allah, this wording in the hadith presents no extremism of any kind. But only one enlightened by the correct meanings of words understands the soundness and correctness of the wording, not the pretentious, tempted ignoramus who follows his desires, who has in himself the love of rising above people though he is one of them and no higher than them; but these are the concepts of the righteous only, not of fools.""")

